Q: How to speed up bulk insertion of pairs into a std::map? A: <p>A simple way to speed u bulk insertion into a map is ;</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Sort the input by key</p>
</li>
<li><p>Use hinted insertion so the map can insert each element after the previous one</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>This reduces the number of tree rotations and rebalancing operations.</p>
<p>Example:</p>
<pre><code>// generate random pairs
std::vector&lt;std::pair&lt;size_t, size_t&gt;&gt; vins(100000);
    for (auto&amp; p : vins) {
    p.first = rand() % 1000000;
    p.second = rand() % 2;
}


clock_t t0 = clock();

// sort by key
std::sort(vins.begin(), vins.end(),
[](auto&amp; a, auto&amp; b){ return a.first &lt; b.first; });

// hinted insertion
std::map&lt;size_t, size_t&gt; m;
auto hint = m.begin();
for (auto&amp; p : vins) {
    hint = m.insert(hint, p);
}
</code></pre>

Q: How can I make a &quot;composer run dev&quot; equivalent with Laravel Sail? A: <p>Laravel Sail doesn’t have a built-in “composer run dev” equivalent for multiple long-running processes.</p>
<p>The simplest approach is to run them together using concurrently (recommended):</p>
<p><strong>1. Install concurrently</strong></p>
<pre><code>npm install concurrently --save-dev
</code></pre>
<p><strong>2. Update package.json</strong></p>
<pre><code>{
  &quot;scripts&quot;: {
    &quot;dev&quot;: &quot;concurrently \&quot;npm run dev\&quot; \&quot;php artisan queue:work\&quot; \&quot;php artisan reverb:start\&quot;&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>3. Run with Sail</strong></p>
<pre><code>sail npm run dev
</code></pre>
<p>This keeps everything in one command and works cleanly with Sail without needing Docker overrides.</p>

